    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1476">

                <pb facs="1117" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1001"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/214.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department informed Colonel Borboa, Villista commander San Luis Potosí,
                    threatening confiscation foreign mining property and imposition forced loan upon
                    foreigners, within five days.</p>
                <p>In calling this particular case to General Villa’s immediate attention request
                    him to issue general instructions to his commanders directing them to respect
                    foreign rights and property. Such an order from General Villa would obviate
                    repeated representations, save trouble and enable foreigners to enjoy with
                    greater security the guarantees which they are entitled to and should have.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
